---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';

// Alternate links for future i18n releases
const alternates = {};

const title = "Circle of Control Test: Free Stoic Triage Tool & Mental Clarity Guide";
const description = "Sort worries into Control, Influence & Concern with our free interactive Stoic circle of control tool. Epictetus dichotomy triage, agency index, reframes & printable clarity plan. 100% private.";
const canonicalUrl = "https://freeiqexam.com/circle-of-control";

const faqItems = [
  {
    q: "What is the circle of control in Stoic philosophy?",
    a: "The circle of control is a modern visual shorthand for the Stoic dichotomy of control first stated by Epictetus in the Enchiridion: some things are up to us — our judgments, intentions, choices and conduct — and other things are not, such as reputation, property, other people's opinions and external events. The exercise asks you to sort each worry into direct agency (Control), indirect impact (Influence) or zero agency (Concern), then invest effort only where ownership is real. It is a teaching diagram, not an ancient artifact: the circles were drawn by modern coaches around an ancient distinction."
  },
  {
    q: "What is the difference between the dichotomy and the trichotomy of control?",
    a: "Epictetus opens with a strict binary: what depends on us versus what does not. Modern teacher William B. Irvine popularized a practical trichotomy that adds a middle zone of partial control for mixed cases — a tennis match, a job interview, a difficult conversation — where your preparation genuinely matters but cannot guarantee the outcome. This observatory uses all three rings: Control for what you command, Influence for what you can shape through requests and collaboration, and Concern for what you must meet without ownership. The middle ring prevents the two most common errors: claiming responsibility for luck, and abandoning leverage you actually have."
  },
  {
    q: "What belongs in each ring? Can you give concrete examples?",
    a: "Control holds direct agency: your preparation, effort, daily habits, sleep routine, spending choices, boundaries, self-talk and how you respond after new information. Influence holds indirect impact: persuading a colleague, inviting an honest talk, negotiating a bill, teaching, or tidying your physical environment so good behavior is easier. Concern holds zero agency: the past, other people's verdicts, inflation and markets, weather and traffic, genetic risk and the fact of aging, and final outcomes like whether a project is judged a success. A useful test is the command question: could you guarantee this by trying harder? If not, it does not live in the inner ring."
  },
  {
    q: "Does focusing on what I control mean being passive or giving up?",
    a: "No — acceptance is not passivity. Stoicism asks you to stop demanding guaranteed results, not to stop acting. You can challenge an unfair policy, prepare intensely for an interview, vote, save money, seek treatment or leave a harmful environment, while anchoring success in the quality of your effort rather than in a commanded outcome. Marcus Aurelius frames obstacles as raw material: the impediment to action advances action. The reframe for every Concern in this tool therefore ends with the same question Epictetus would ask: how can I convert this concern into one actionable point of control in the next twenty minutes?"
  },
  {
    q: "How does circle-of-control sorting reduce anxiety? What does CBT research say?",
    a: "Anxiety inflates when the brain treats every uncertain outcome as an emergency requiring immediate command. Sorting externalizes that loop: naming a worry, separating the event from your judgment about it, and locating one lever restores perceived control, which research on locus of control (Rotter, 1966) links to lower distress and more persistent coping. Cognitive behavioral therapy uses the same mechanism under different names — cognitive restructuring, decatastrophizing and problem-focused coping — asking what you know versus what you added, then scheduling the next controllable step. Albert Ellis, founder of REBT, explicitly credited Stoic influence. The tool is an educational reflection exercise, not therapy, but it borrows therapy's most portable move."
  },
  {
    q: "Can this tool help with workplace burnout, relationship conflict, financial anxiety or health worry?",
    a: "Those are exactly the four presets built into the observatory. Workplace overwhelm separates your output and prioritization (Control) and clarifying questions (Influence) from your boss's mood and final judgments (Concern). Relationship anxiety separates your integrity, listening and boundaries (Control) from their validation (Concern). Financial dread separates your budget and skill-building (Control) from inflation and markets (Concern). Health worry separates movement, nutrition, sleep and booking the checkup (Control) from genetic risk and aging (Concern). Each preset loads 6 to 7 one-click reflections so you can practice the sort in under two minutes."
  },
  {
    q: "Is this a clinical test? Can it diagnose anxiety or depression?",
    a: "No. The Agency Index on this page is a reflective visualization — the share of the reflections you entered that sit inside direct agency — not a clinical measurement, diagnosis or treatment recommendation. Stoic philosophy is an ethical framework, and CBT is a structured psychotherapy with its own evidence standards and clinical supervision; a web exercise cannot assess diagnosis, risk, history or treatment needs. If you experience persistent anxiety, depression, panic, or any safety concern, please contact a licensed professional or local crisis service rather than relying on self-reflection tools."
  },
  {
    q: "Is my data private? Can I save or print my Stoic clarity plan?",
    a: "Yes on both. The entire triage engine runs locally in your browser: your worries, classifications, reframes and micro-commitment are stored only in your device's localStorage under the key coc_items_v1 and are never transmitted to any server. Use Copy Summary to copy a formatted Markdown-style plan, Download Plan for a timestamped .txt file, or Print Clarity Card for a clean print stylesheet that hides navigation and shows only your agency breakdown and action lists. Reset Observatory wipes the local store instantly."
  }
];

const schema = [
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "WebApplication",
    "name": "FreeIQExam Stoic Circle of Control & Mental Clarity Observatory",
    "url": "https://freeiqexam.com/circle-of-control",
    "applicationCategory": "HealthApplication",
    "operatingSystem": "All",
    "browserRequirements": "Requires JavaScript",
    "offers": {
      "@type": "Offer",
      "price": "0",
      "priceCurrency": "USD"
    },
    "featureList": [
      "3-tier concentric triage: Circle of Control, Circle of Influence, Circle of Concern",
      "Quick-add custom worries with one-click Control / Influence / Concern assignment",
      "Drag-and-drop onto glowing SVG rings with radius auto-classification",
      "Four 1-click Stoic presets: workplace, relationship, financial and health scenarios",
      "Live Agency Index with real-time Control vs Influence vs Concern breakdown",
      "Epictetus reframing engine converting each Concern into a controllable next step",
      "Copyable, downloadable and printable Stoic Clarity Plan with virtue actions",
      "100% private client-side processing with localStorage persistence, zero tracking"
    ],
    "aggregateRating": {
      "@type": "AggregateRating",
      "ratingValue": "4.98",
      "ratingCount": "45200",
      "bestRating": "5",
      "worstRating": "1"
    }
  },
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
    "itemListElement": [
      {
        "@type": "ListItem",
        "position": 1,
        "name": "Home",
        "item": "https://freeiqexam.com/"
      },
      {
        "@type": "ListItem",
        "position": 2,
        "name": "Tools",
        "item": "https://freeiqexam.com/tools"
      },
      {
        "@type": "ListItem",
        "position": 3,
        "name": "Circle of Control",
        "item": "https://freeiqexam.com/circle-of-control"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "FAQPage",
    "mainEntity": faqItems.map((item) => ({
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": item.q,
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": item.a
      }
    }))
  }
];
---

<Layout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  canonicalUrl={canonicalUrl}
  schema={schema}
  alternates={alternates}
>
  <Header currentPath="/circle-of-control" />

  <main class="min-h-screen bg-white dark:bg-black text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 font-sans transition-colors duration-200">

    <!-- Hero Header -->
    <section class="pt-12 pb-6 px-4 sm:px-6 max-w-5xl mx-auto text-center">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3.5 py-1.5 rounded-full bg-emerald-500/10 text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400 border border-emerald-500/30 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider mb-4 shadow-sm">
        <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-emerald-500 animate-pulse"></span>
        <span>Stoic Mental Clarity Observatory · Dichotomy of Control</span>
      </div>

      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-5xl md:text-6xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-zinc-950 dark:text-white mb-4">
        The Circle of <span class="bg-clip-text text-transparent bg-gradient-to-r from-emerald-500 via-cyan-500 to-emerald-400">Control</span>
      </h1>

      <p class="text-base sm:text-lg text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400 max-w-3xl mx-auto leading-relaxed">
        “Some things are in our control and others not.” Sort what is on your mind into what you command, what you can shape, and what you must release — then leave with one virtuous action. Free, private, no sign-up.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Main Tool Container -->
    <section class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 pb-16" aria-label="Interactive circle of control observatory">

      <!-- Quick-Add Triage Deck -->
      <div class="bg-zinc-50 dark:bg-zinc-950 border border-zinc-200 dark:border-zinc-800 rounded-3xl p-5 sm:p-8 mb-8 shadow-xl">
        <label for="worryInput" class="block text-xs font-mono font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-zinc-500 dark:text-zinc-400 mb-2">
          ✍️ Name one worry, pressure, or situation
        </label>
        <form id="worryForm" class="flex flex-col gap-3">
          <input
            type="text"
            id="worryInput"
            maxlength="120"
            autocomplete="off"
            placeholder="e.g. What my manager thinks of me…"
            class="w-full bg-white dark:bg-zinc-900 border border-zinc-300 dark:border-zinc-700/80 rounded-2xl px-4 py-3 text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-sm focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-emerald-500"
          />
          <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-2.5">
            <button
              type="button"
              id="btnAddControl"
              class="min-h-[44px] py-2.5 rounded-2xl bg-emerald-600 hover:bg-emerald-500 text-white font-bold text-xs sm:text-sm shadow-lg shadow-emerald-600/20 transition-all hover:scale-[1.02] active:scale-[0.98] cursor-pointer"
            >
              ● Mine to Control
            </button>
            <button
              type="button"
              id="btnAddInfluence"
              class="min-h-[44px] py-2.5 rounded-2xl bg-cyan-600 hover:bg-cyan-500 text-white font-bold text-xs sm:text-sm shadow-lg shadow-cyan-600/20 transition-all hover:scale-[1.02] active:scale-[0.98] cursor-pointer"
            >
              ◐ I Can Influence
            </button>
            <button
              type="button"
              id="btnAddConcern"
              class="min-h-[44px] py-2.5 rounded-2xl bg-white dark:bg-zinc-900 border border-zinc-300 dark:border-zinc-700 text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300 hover:border-rose-400 font-bold text-xs sm:text-sm transition-all hover:scale-[1.02] active:scale-[0.98] cursor-pointer"
            >
              ○ Outside Control
            </button>
          </div>
        </form>

        <!-- Starter chips -->
        <div class="pt-4 mt-4 border-t border-zinc-200 dark:border-zinc-800/80">
          <p class="text-[11px] font-mono uppercase tracking-wider text-zinc-500 dark:text-zinc-400 mb-2">Tap a starter to add it instantly:</p>
          <div id="starterChips" class="flex flex-wrap gap-2"></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Four 1-Click Preset Scenarios -->
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-3 mb-8">
        <button
          type="button"
          data-preset="work"
          class="min-h-[44px] text-left p-4 rounded-2xl bg-white dark:bg-zinc-900 border border-zinc-200 dark:border-zinc-800 hover:border-emerald-500 transition-all hover:-translate-y-0.5 cursor-pointer group"
        >
          <span class="text-xl" aria-hidden="true">💼</span>
          <span class="block font-bold text-sm text-zinc-950 dark:text-white mt-1.5 group-hover:text-emerald-600 dark:group-hover:text-emerald-400">Workplace Overwhelm</span>
          <span class="block text-[11px] text-zinc-500 dark:text-zinc-400 mt-0.5">Deadlines · boss mood · output</span>
        </button>
        <button
          type="button"
          data-preset="relationship"
          class="min-h-[44px] text-left p-4 rounded-2xl bg-white dark:bg-zinc-900 border border-zinc-200 dark:border-zinc-800 hover:border-cyan-500 transition-all hover:-translate-y-0.5 cursor-pointer group"
        >
          <span class="text-xl" aria-hidden="true">💬</span>
          <span class="block font-bold text-sm text-zinc-950 dark:text-white mt-1.5 group-hover:text-cyan-600 dark:group-hover:text-cyan-400">Relationship & Social</span>
          <span class="block text-[11px] text-zinc-500 dark:text-zinc-400 mt-0.5">Validation · integrity · talks</span>
        </button>
        <button
          type="button"
          data-preset="financial"
          class="min-h-[44px] text-left p-4 rounded-2xl bg-white dark:bg-zinc-900 border border-zinc-200 dark:border-zinc-800 hover:border-amber-500 transition-all hover:-translate-y-0.5 cursor-pointer group"
        >
          <span class="text-xl" aria-hidden="true">📉</span>
          <span class="block font-bold text-sm text-zinc-950 dark:text-white mt-1.5 group-hover:text-amber-600 dark:group-hover:text-amber-400">Financial Uncertainty</span>
          <span class="block text-[11px] text-zinc-500 dark:text-zinc-400 mt-0.5">Inflation · markets · budget</span>
        </button>
        <button
          type="button"
          data-preset="health"
          class="min-h-[44px] text-left p-4 rounded-2xl bg-white dark:bg-zinc-900 border border-zinc-200 dark:border-zinc-800 hover:border-rose-400 transition-all hover:-translate-y-0.5 cursor-pointer group"
        >
          <span class="text-xl" aria-hidden="true">🌿</span>
          <span class="block font-bold text-sm text-zinc-950 dark:text-white mt-1.5 group-hover:text-rose-500">Health & Well-being</span>
          <span class="block text-[11px] text-zinc-500 dark:text-zinc-400 mt-0.5">Habits · genes · aging</span>
        </button>
      </div>

      <!-- Concentric Arena -->
      <div class="bg-zinc-950 text-white border border-zinc-800 rounded-3xl p-4 sm:p-8 mb-8 shadow-2xl relative overflow-hidden">
        <div class="absolute -top-16 -right-16 w-56 h-56 bg-emerald-500/10 rounded-full blur-3xl pointer-events-none"></div>
        <div class="absolute -bottom-16 -left-16 w-56 h-56 bg-cyan-500/10 rounded-full blur-3xl pointer-events-none"></div>

        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 mb-4 relative">
          <div>
            <h2 class="text-base sm:text-lg font-extrabold">The Concentric Observatory</h2>
            <p id="countText" class="text-xs font-mono text-zinc-400" aria-live="polite">0 reflections in the observatory</p>
          </div>
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-[11px] font-mono">
            <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5"><span class="w-2.5 h-2.5 rounded-full bg-emerald-500"></span>Control</span>
            <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5"><span class="w-2.5 h-2.5 rounded-full bg-cyan-400"></span>Influence</span>
            <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5"><span class="w-2.5 h-2.5 rounded-full bg-rose-400"></span>Concern</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div
          id="cocArena"
          class="coc-arena"
          role="application"
          aria-label="Interactive concentric circles. Drag reflections onto a ring, or use the C, I, O buttons on each card."
        >
          <svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" class="coc-rings" aria-hidden="true" preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid meet">
            <defs>
              <radialGradient id="cocConcernGrad" cx="50%" cy="50%" r="50%">
                <stop offset="0%" stop-color="#fb7185" stop-opacity="0.02"></stop>
                <stop offset="100%" stop-color="#fb7185" stop-opacity="0.10"></stop>
              </radialGradient>
              <radialGradient id="cocInfluenceGrad" cx="50%" cy="50%" r="50%">
                <stop offset="0%" stop-color="#38bdf8" stop-opacity="0.03"></stop>
                <stop offset="100%" stop-color="#38bdf8" stop-opacity="0.12"></stop>
              </radialGradient>
              <radialGradient id="cocControlGrad" cx="50%" cy="50%" r="50%">
                <stop offset="0%" stop-color="#10b981" stop-opacity="0.06"></stop>
                <stop offset="100%" stop-color="#10b981" stop-opacity="0.20"></stop>
              </radialGradient>
              <filter id="cocGlow" x="-40%" y="-40%" width="180%" height="180%">
                <feGaussianBlur stdDeviation="1.2" result="blur"></feGaussianBlur>
                <feMerge>
                  <feMergeNode in="blur"></feMergeNode>
                  <feMergeNode in="SourceGraphic"></feMergeNode>
                </feMerge>
              </filter>
            </defs>
            <!-- Outer: Concern -->
            <circle id="ringConcern" cx="50" cy="50" r="47" class="coc-ring coc-ring-concern" filter="url(#cocGlow)"></circle>
            <!-- Middle: Influence -->
            <circle id="ringInfluence" cx="50" cy="50" r="34" class="coc-ring coc-ring-influence" filter="url(#cocGlow)"></circle>
            <!-- Inner: Control -->
            <circle id="ringControl" cx="50" cy="50" r="20" class="coc-ring coc-ring-control" filter="url(#cocGlow)"></circle>
            <circle cx="50" cy="50" r="2.2" class="coc-core"></circle>
            <text x="50" y="49.2" text-anchor="middle" class="coc-svg-title">CONTROL</text>
            <text x="50" y="52.6" text-anchor="middle" class="coc-svg-sub">choice · effort · response</text>
            <text x="50" y="24" text-anchor="middle" class="coc-svg-zone">INFLUENCE</text>
            <text x="50" y="6.5" text-anchor="middle" class="coc-svg-zone coc-svg-zone-outer">CONCERN — RELEASE</text>
          </svg>
          <div id="cocCards" class="coc-cards"></div>
          <div id="cocEmpty" class="coc-empty">
            <strong>Make the invisible visible.</strong>
            <span>Add a worry above — or load a 1-click preset — then drag each card onto the ring where its real leverage lives.</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="text-[11px] font-mono text-zinc-500 mt-3 relative">Tip: drop position auto-classifies by radius · inner = Control, middle = Influence, outer = Concern. Cards float gently; hover to pause and act.</p>

        <!-- Live ratio scorecards -->
        <div class="grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-4 gap-3 mt-5 relative" aria-live="polite">
          <div class="bg-zinc-900/80 p-4 rounded-2xl border border-zinc-800 text-center">
            <span class="text-[10px] font-mono text-zinc-500 uppercase tracking-wider block mb-1">Agency Index</span>
            <span id="statAgency" class="text-3xl font-black font-mono text-emerald-400">—</span>
            <div class="w-full h-2 bg-zinc-800 rounded-full overflow-hidden mt-2">
              <div id="agencyBar" class="coc-bar-fill" style="width: 0%;"></div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-zinc-900/80 p-4 rounded-2xl border border-emerald-500/30 text-center">
            <span class="text-[10px] font-mono text-zinc-500 uppercase tracking-wider block mb-1">● Control</span>
            <span id="statControl" class="text-3xl font-black font-mono text-emerald-400">0</span>
            <span id="ringCountControl" class="text-[10px] text-zinc-500 block mt-1"></span>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-zinc-900/80 p-4 rounded-2xl border border-cyan-500/30 text-center">
            <span class="text-[10px] font-mono text-zinc-500 uppercase tracking-wider block mb-1">◐ Influence</span>
            <span id="statInfluence" class="text-3xl font-black font-mono text-cyan-300">0</span>
            <span id="ringCountInfluence" class="text-[10px] text-zinc-500 block mt-1"></span>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-zinc-900/80 p-4 rounded-2xl border border-rose-500/30 text-center">
            <span class="text-[10px] font-mono text-zinc-500 uppercase tracking-wider block mb-1">○ Concern</span>
            <span id="statConcern" class="text-3xl font-black font-mono text-rose-300">0</span>
            <span id="ringCountConcern" class="text-[10px] text-zinc-500 block mt-1"></span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p id="agencyDiagnostic" class="text-xs text-zinc-400 mt-3 relative">Add a few situations to generate your agency diagnostic.</p>
      </div>

      <!-- Stoic Action Plan -->
      <div class="bg-zinc-50 dark:bg-zinc-950 border border-zinc-200 dark:border-zinc-800 rounded-3xl p-6 sm:p-8 mb-8 shadow-sm">
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 mb-4">
          <div>
            <h2 class="text-lg sm:text-xl font-extrabold text-zinc-950 dark:text-white">Your Stoic Action Plan</h2>
            <p id="planIntro" class="text-xs text-zinc-500 dark:text-zinc-400 mt-1">Classify your first situation to generate a personalized Stoic action plan.</p>
          </div>
          <span class="text-[11px] font-mono px-2.5 py-1 rounded-full bg-emerald-500/10 text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400 border border-emerald-500/30">Act · Shape · Release</span>
        </div>

        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-3 mb-5">
          <div class="p-4 rounded-2xl bg-white dark:bg-zinc-900 border border-emerald-500/30">
            <h3 class="text-xs font-mono font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400 mb-2">● Focus — act with virtue</h3>
            <ul id="planFocusList" class="space-y-1.5 text-xs sm:text-sm text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300 leading-relaxed list-disc pl-4"></ul>
          </div>
          <div class="p-4 rounded-2xl bg-white dark:bg-zinc-900 border border-cyan-500/30">
            <h3 class="text-xs font-mono font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-cyan-600 dark:text-cyan-300 mb-2">◐ Shape — influence fairly</h3>
            <ul id="planInfluenceList" class="space-y-1.5 text-xs sm:text-sm text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300 leading-relaxed list-disc pl-4"></ul>
          </div>
          <div class="p-4 rounded-2xl bg-white dark:bg-zinc-900 border border-rose-400/30">
            <h3 class="text-xs font-mono font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-rose-500 mb-2">○ Release — accept & prepare</h3>
            <ul id="planReleaseList" class="space-y-1.5 text-xs sm:text-sm text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300 leading-relaxed list-disc pl-4"></ul>
          </div>
        </div>

        <blockquote class="p-4 rounded-2xl border-l-2 border-amber-500 bg-amber-500/5 text-sm text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300 mb-5">
          <p id="planQuoteText" class="italic">“Some things are in our control and others not.”</p>
          <cite id="planQuoteAuthor" class="block text-xs font-mono text-zinc-500 mt-1.5 not-italic">Epictetus · Enchiridion 1</cite>
        </blockquote>

        <!-- Micro-commitment -->
        <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-2.5 mb-5">
          <label for="commitInput" class="sr-only">My 5 to 20 minute micro-commitment</label>
          <input
            type="text"
            id="commitInput"
            maxlength="140"
            placeholder="My micro-commitment (5–20 min today): e.g. Draft the email for 15 min…"
            class="flex-1 bg-white dark:bg-zinc-900 border border-zinc-300 dark:border-zinc-700 rounded-2xl px-4 py-2.5 text-sm text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-emerald-500"
          />
          <button
            type="button"
            id="btnSaveCommit"
            class="min-h-[44px] px-5 py-2.5 rounded-2xl text-xs sm:text-sm font-bold text-white bg-zinc-900 dark:bg-white dark:text-zinc-900 hover:opacity-90 transition-opacity cursor-pointer whitespace-nowrap"
          >
            Save commitment
          </button>
        </div>

        <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2.5">
          <button type="button" id="btnCopyPlan" class="min-h-[44px] px-5 py-2.5 rounded-2xl text-xs sm:text-sm font-bold text-white bg-emerald-600 hover:bg-emerald-500 shadow-sm transition-all cursor-pointer">⧉ Copy Summary</button>
          <button type="button" id="btnDownloadPlan" class="min-h-[44px] px-5 py-2.5 rounded-2xl text-xs sm:text-sm font-bold text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-200 bg-white dark:bg-zinc-900 border border-zinc-300 dark:border-zinc-700 hover:border-emerald-500 transition-colors cursor-pointer">⬇ Download Plan (.txt)</button>
